# Environments
# .env is committed as template, .env.local contains secrets
.env.local
.envrc
.venv
# The mount point a contained session's environment is bound at. The engine
# creates it inside the bind, which is this tree, so it stands here on the
# host as an empty directory whether or not a container is running.
#
# No trailing slash, so the name is ignored whatever it is. With one this
# matched only a directory, and a worktree that reached its sibling's
# environment by symlinking the same name had that symlink committed —
# `git add -A` saw a file the rule did not cover.
.venv-contained
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

