marimo/_static/
marimo/_lsp/
__marimo__/

# Project-specific
# lup: template: does this domain commit its session data? Traces, outputs and
# feedback rounds stay local by default; a domain whose runs yield an artifact
# worth versioning removes the notes/* and !notes/.gitkeep pair below, which is
# the commit-loop decision /lup:init walks. The notes/harness/ line under them
# is a separate answer, and the default there is no.
notes/*
!notes/.gitkeep
# That answer is no because the harness store holds a different kind of thing
# from the rest of notes/. Everything else there is what this project's own runs
# produced -- sessions, outputs, logs, feedback rounds -- filed under the agent
# version that produced them, read back by the feedback loop, and worth
# versioning wherever a domain wants its results to have a history. This holds
# one directory per `lup-devtools harness <runtime>` launch, each an
# observable.jsonl mirroring an operator's interactive session with a native CLI
# as it happens: filed under a timestamp, redacted for portability rather than
# for publication, read back by nothing here, and reaching hundreds of megabytes
# within days. A domain that does want those versioned deletes this line, having
# answered a question the one above it never asked.
# Not notes/traces/<version>/sessions/harness/, which is a different store: the
# session a natively launched tool server opens, inside the trace store like
# every other session, and covered by the pair above like every other trace.
notes/harness/
worktrees/
tmp/
.lup/
# The gate's generated Pyright configuration. It has to sit at the root, since
# Pyright resolves a base's relative includes against the file that declares
# them, and `dev check` unlinks it — but a run that is killed rather than
# returned from never reaches that line. `sweep_pyright_scratch` takes those
# once they are old enough to be nobody's; this is what stops one being
# committed before the sweep is due. One already was, in f289dca35, carrying
# an absolute path to a worktree that no longer exists.
.lup-pyright-*.json
sync.json.local
downstream.json.local
# Personal harness config, one per native tree; the generated siblings are committed.
.claude/settings.local.json
.codex/config.local.toml
# The machine's own overlay beside each tree — `/lup:profile` naming the
# profiles this machine keeps — rendered by every generation and launch.
.claude/plugins/local/
.codex/skills/
.cache/
refs/
**/*.bak
# A native runtime's write journal, which it makes beside whichever directory
# it was reading — including inside the library's own package root, where an
# empty `.claude/` is the first thing a newcomer scanning that tree meets.
**/.cc-writes/
# The frontend workspace: dependencies restored from the lockfile, types
# compiled from the view schema at build, and Vite's scratch output. The built
# bundles are committed, under lup.web's package data, as a generated tree.
packages/lup/web/node_modules/
packages/lup/web/src/generated/
packages/lup/web/out/
